 "what_changed_from_the_first_matrix": {
  "first_receipt_gain_pct": -99.51525523716245,
  "this_receipt_gain_pct": -4.692052097581123,
  "detail": "The first full matrix read -99.5152%. This one reads -4.6921% on the same generation, the same policy and the same box, and the difference is entirely in the ruler:\n  * The packed-path guard divided decode steps by a count that includes prefill chunks, so `ctx4096-c16` and `ctx4096-c32` were refused although every decode step batched at full width. Both are measured here.\n  * `ctx4096-c4` and `ctx16384-c4` genuinely cannot be batched by this runtime -- a probe with no policy running reproduces max_rows_seen 0 at two decode lengths -- so they are attributed to the runtime, not scored, and the receipt is PARTIAL on its face.\n  * `ctx128-c32` reached the generation's cell floor last time on a p99 whose calibrated control spread is 481%. It does not this time.\nNo cell is at the floor in this receipt."
 },
 "findings": [
  {
   "finding": "Eight cells scored, eight negative, none improved.",
   "detail": "Goodput: -0.290% at ctx128-c1, -0.272% at ctx128-c4, -0.409% at ctx128-c16, -1.103% at ctx128-c32, -0.180% at ctx4096-c1, -0.754% at ctx4096-c16, -6.667% at ctx4096-c32 and -0.444% at ctx16384-c1. Five of the eight resolve against the spread the generation published for that cell. The shipped default policy is a regression wherever this instrument can see it."
  },
  {
   "finding": "The scheduling-outlier detector, built this morning from ONE instance, caught two more.",
   "detail": "`ctx128-c32` repeat 1 at 9.53x its group's non-decode step count (576.9 tok/s against a group median of 887.7) and `ctx4096-c32` repeat 3 at 4.6x (118.0 against 168.0). Both are the runtime scheduling requests serially, both pass every other guard, and the second is most of why ctx4096-c32 reads -6.667%. Scored and named rather than refused, because the failure is the runtime's -- but a three-repeat median does not survive one of them, which is exactly what the receipt says on its face."
  },
  {
   "finding": "The probe inside this run returned UNHOOKED, which was a defect in the runner.",
   "detail": "`ATTRIBUTION_ENV` did not set `RECURLOCAL_STATS`, so the probe emitted no telemetry, the harness refused it as unhooked, and UNHOOKED is not a serving guard -- so both cells came back attributed to the candidate and stayed charged. Conservative and useless. Fixed. The verdicts recorded here come from the dedicated probe of the same two cells on the same box, which did set it."
  }
